  "about": "Jambot's swing axis: one value s in 0..1 drives two levels of a 4/4 bar. swingParts(s) gives each level's lean (eighth = clamp(2s - 1), sixteenth = clamp(2s) * (1 - eighth)), shareOfLean turns a lean into the share of its span the first half holds (0.5 straight, 2/3 at a lean of 1), and swingMap(s) = leanMap(swingParts(s)) places the bar's sixteen sixteenths: onsets[k] is where the k-th is played, in sixteenths from the downbeat (a beat is 4).",
  "how": "Written by running swingParts, swingShares and swingMap of that file for s = i / 20, i = 0 … 20.",
